{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/256473-storm-lords-ban","id":256473,"title":"Storm Lords Ban","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-13T21:50:39-07:00","id":256473,"title":"Storm Lords Ban","content":"So first off I want to apologize to every werewolf player seeing this sort of thread yet again. I have searched online and through old archives but haven't been able to find any of the old threads discussing this topic, but I do remember the discussions being very interesting and offering some new insight into one of my favorite tribes.<br /> <br /> So with that out of the way I was wanting to ask you all about how you interpret the Storm Lords' ban, &quot;allow no one to witness or tend to your weakness&quot;. A very lofty ban nearly up there with the ones the Pure have to put up with in my opinion. But I imagine I'm falling into the trap of taking this ban a little too literally, but that's the issue with these bans that leave so much room for interpretation.<br /> <br /> Do you think Storm Lords aren't allowed to ever relax around their packmates? Do you think shedding tears goes against their ban? Or do you think Winter Wolf's ban is leveled against more serious issues that could genuinely threaten the pack? And if so where do you draw the line?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2322-star-sage","name":"Star Sage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2322_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T22:12:35-07:00","id":256521,"title":"","content":"Hopefully this will help. It is an excerpt of the Storm Lords from the upcoming W:TF 2e<br /> <br /> This story is true. After the murder of Father Wolf, when the Forsaken were scattered like grains across the earth and hunted by flesh and spirit alike, a clever hunter chased a monster. The monster was stronger than the hunter, but the hunter endured its blows, though they tore her flesh and spilled her blood. The monster was faster than the hunter, but when the monster stopped to rest the hunter pressed on, though her muscles ached and her very bones were weary. At last she chased the hunter up a great mountain, where the bitter cold froze it stiff and slowed its pace so that the hunter caught up. After a great battle, the monster was slain, but the hunter was mortally wounded. It was then that <i>Skolis-Ur</i> emerged from his den, drawn by the noise of battle. He offered to bind the hunter\u2019s wounds, but she refused and packed them with snow to numb the pain. He offered to carry her down the mountain, but she refused and began the torturous climb herself. When she could walk no farther, he offered to end her pain, but she refused and lingered for a full day and night before dying. As her spirit rose from her body, <i>Skolis-Ur</i> bowed his head in respect and said, \u201chere is a true scion of <i>Urfarah</i>.\u201d It is from this tale that we take our Oath: \u201cAllow no one to witness or to tend your weakness.\u201d<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T22:13:23-07:00","id":256523,"title":"","content":"Do you have Tribes of the Moon? Because it goes into this better than I can, but here we go. Basically, weakness as defined by the ban is anything that disadvantages you or your packmates; that puts you into danger and gets in the way of what has to be done. If someone murders your family, you're not supposed to just stand there and take it. You're expected to get angry, and yeah, to cry a bit, and then go rip the bastard's head off. Witnessing weakness: be an inspiration to your pack, don't let them see you fail. Tending to your weakness: your failings are your own to bear, don't let your pack help you with it. Being a Storm Lord is about serving as an example. Let your pack see you stumble, but don't let them see you fall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T09:49:37-07:00","id":256687,"title":"","content":"On a more strategic level, you could try to interpret it as 'keep your cards close to your vest' since the less you call attention to your weak points, the less likely you are to have them taken advantage of. Be self-reliant, be responsible enough that you can take care of others instead of needing them to take care of you.<br /> <br /> It can, of course lead to very unsatisfying roleplay if your in-character response is always 'hide in your room until everyone stops asking if you are OK', but I also like the potential discord in being a non-'alpha' storm lord, because you end up supporting the leader or inspiring your elders with your example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T10:57:49-07:00","id":256706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/256473-storm-lords-ban?p=256687#post256687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can, of course lead to very unsatisfying roleplay if your in-character response is always 'hide in your room until everyone stops asking if you are OK.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that hiding in your room every time would be considered a violation of the oath since they would associate it with weakness. I believe the best summary we have so far in this thread is from Merkonan with your failings are your own to bear, don't let your pack help you with it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T12:26:30-07:00","id":256753,"title":"","content":"It isn't realistic to be completely unphased by hardships though... There has to be some way you process or work through the problems you deal with. Definitely not disagreeing with Merkonan, but the question of when you are breaking your ban goes into a bit of a spiral if smaller and smaller coping mechanisms are ban-breaking, no?<br /> <br /> Just because you perform as the ideal for your pack to uphold doesn't mean you can do so 24/7 without some sort of dramatic failure down the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T12:50:38-07:00","id":256759,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd be very leery to take the Storm Lord's ban as to requiring the character to never seek help. It promotes the &quot;Lone Wolf&quot; archetype and I find that to be damaging to games where you're meant to operate in a Pack. Further, it restricts the capacity of other players to have their characters useful. The Storm Lord should be able to consult the Pack's Cahalith and Itheaur regarding emotional and mental issues so that those two Auspices can actually do their jobs in the Pack and demanding that the Storm Lord's ban prohibits that, I feel introduces issues into the game that should not be welcomed or encouraged.<br /> <br /> Now, I don't have a problem with a specific Storm Lord having an issue asking their packmates for help, but if the writers actually require a Storm Lord to suffer in silence instead of seeking the help they need in order to become better and stronger, then I'm going to be extremely disappointed in the 2nd Ed writers and developer for promoting the toxic environment towards emotional and mental well-being that exists in our society.<br /> <br /> A Storm Lord talking with their Itheaur or Cahalith about their fears and issues in private should be viewed as the Storm Lord tackling their problems and growing stronger for it, because all the Itheaur or Cahalith can do is lend a helpful ear and their opinion, but it'd be the Storm Lord actually standing up in getting better. Skolis-Ur should respect that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 09-14-2014, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T13:18:15-07:00","id":256792,"title":"","content":"Dropping in an assist for Merkonan:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tribes of the Moon, p158</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some people matter. They have the strength to matter to others, to the world. In the span of one heartbeat or the thunder of many, we all get the chance. Maybe just one shot, but it\u2019ll be there. The exhausted paramedic saving a dying baby at a premature home delivery. The bigger kid who helps the beaten child stand up to his bully. The soldier who goes back for his wounded comrade. In life, a single act of strength \u2014 a single moment of courage, of skill, of defiance and endurance \u2014 can be all it takes for a soul to matter.<br /> <br /> People are inspired by those who matter. Those who matter are the ones who change the world, even in the smallest ways.<br /> <br /> <u>Duty.</u> A human word. What\u2019s duty to a man with a wolf\u2019s soul? Pride? Who could ever be proud of a fear of failure? Do you know us at all? It\u2019s not about looking good or winning glory. It\u2019s not about being the biggest, the best or the bravest. It\u2019s about being ready for that one second when you have to matter, that one moment when you can change the world around you for the better.<br /> <br /> Because if you don\u2019t, if you miss that moment, people die. The people you love, the people who need you, the people you swore to inspire and protect will die.<br /> <br /> Be ready for anything. You swore to a wolf-god you\u2019d stand up to all that could ever go wrong without letting your pack down. No matter what the two worlds throw at you, be it anguish or agony, just keep going. Endure where others would surrender. Survive where others would die.<br /> <br /> Bleed when you\u2019re hurt and roar in rage when the world spins against you. You\u2019re not a god or demon, to resist such things with an immortal\u2019s nonchalance. But let the others know you\u2019re not down and you\u2019re not out. Cry out in pain, not despair. The others have to see you\u2019re still standing come the dawn. Let your pack see you walk through hell and come out the other side. Whether you\u2019re laughing or crying, they\u2019ll know they can rely on you, trust you and follow you.<br /> <br /> Inspire them.<br /> <br /> <u>Matter</u> to them.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tribes of the Moon, p159</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldering real responsibility is a tricky duty to manage for anyone, and it gets even harder when someone promises a wolf-god she\u2019ll bear all life\u2019s burdens without letting anyone see her fail. That\u2019s a key point not always remembered: at no point does a werewolf swear to Winter Wolf that she\u2019ll never, ever fail. She swears only that she\u2019ll do all in her power to avoid letting others see her failures, for fear of demoralizing them or breaking their own hopes.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T13:26:32-07:00","id":256796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/256473-storm-lords-ban?p=256687#post256687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can, of course lead to very unsatisfying roleplay if your in-character response is always <i>'hide in your room until everyone stops asking if you are OK</i>', but I also like the potential discord in being a non-'alpha' storm lord, because you end up supporting the leader or inspiring your elders with your example.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to think a true Iminir in such situation would go<b> &quot;YES I'M FUCKING OK, DROP THAT SHIT.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> And non-alpha Iminir strive to be the best at their job. The Iminir creed to to lead by example. An Iminir can be the Omega, but even then he will be an indispensable member of the pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T13:46:14-07:00","id":256809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/256473-storm-lords-ban?p=256796#post256796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like to think a true Iminir in such situation would go<b> &amp;quot;YES I'M FUCKING OK, DROP THAT SHIT.&amp;quot;</b><br /> <br /> And non-alpha Iminir strive to be the best at their job. The Iminir creed to to lead by example. An Iminir can be the Omega, but even then he will be an indispensable member of the pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>That definitely makes sense, it just doesn't sound to me like something you can always manage to do?<br /> <br /> <br /> When Star Sage opened the thread he apologized for this being -another- Imnir thread? Sorry, one of my first too, I like it a lot - learning about how to play the character, anticipating whatever my first WW game will be... So if there is more to say I would love to keep going with it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T19:04:54-07:00","id":256949,"title":"","content":"Just chiming in to say that I agree with the consensus here - I love me some Storm Lords (I'm playing a Storm Lord Elodoth in a 2e playtest, in fact!), and I feel like the Ban must be seen in the context of the Tribe's culture and their Primary Renown of Honour, and most importantly (as 2e does so well), in the context of <b><i>The Hunt</i></b>.<br /> <br /> The Storm Lords are all about duty; modelling and embodying it at all times, whether to others outside the Tribe, others within the Tribe, or just to themselves. They aren't just jocks and tough-guys - they know that weakness at the wrong time could mean failure in The Hunt and death for their loved ones, so they have built a culture that resists it at every turn. It's not about being the toughest or hiding the fact that you failed a roll - it is about a culture of being dependable, honourable, reliable. The Storm Lords Will. Not. Fail. You.<br /> <br /> And I'd say that their Prey figures into the equation, too - they police the border between the worlds. They need to be the fearsome, fearless, unstoppable, irresistible monsters, or the spirits will slip the chains and run amok. They must show their prey no weakness, or it will be exploited.<br /> <br /> So, in light of this, what would a Storm Lord feel is transgressing their Ban? I would say the main thing is <i>anything that endangers the hunt</i>. Letting your mundane life distract you from your duty is showing weakness of personality. Just getting wounded, or needing medical attention, isn't a transgression - but as soon as you're well enough to stand, you damn well better be out patrolling again, even if it's just to let your packmates know if you find something. Sobbing with rage when your partner is cut down in front of you is not a sin, but giving up on getting revenge because the foe seems undefeatable certainly is. Realising that you can't take an opponent one-on-one isn't shameful (my character is Physical tertiary, myself), but letting that be the end of it reeks of cowardice. Just having a particular weakness isn't the end of the world (no one has a &quot;5&quot; in everything, after all), but <i>letting it get in the way</i> is.<br /> <br /> So, TL;DR - I would say that it is all about Your Duty. You must show others what it looks like to be the ever-vigilant hunter. You, yourself, must not endanger The Hunt. You must not fail.<br /> <br /> (Easy, right?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T20:38:07-07:00","id":256966,"title":"","content":"Well said!!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T01:30:28-07:00","id":257055,"title":"","content":"Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> And personally, I like that the Storm Lords' Ban is arguably the hardest to keep, too (but then again, I'm a sucker for punishment.) My playtest character is still making up for a failure in her past, and struggling with divided loyalties threatening to tear her away from the hunt. That, to me, is what playing a Storm Lord is *all about*.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T04:56:54-07:00","id":257201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NateD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/256473-storm-lords-ban?p=257055#post257055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*condensed awesome*</div> </div> </div> </div>Very well-said! Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T02:40:37-07:00","id":257990,"title":"","content":"Really happy to see all these great replies about this topic. On Merkonan's point I actually plan on getting my hands on the Tribes of the Moon book and taking a deeper look at the tribes there. I also really love NateD's take on the Storm Lords. I'm pretty much in the camp of &quot;don't let your shortcomings impede your pack or your duty&quot; as far as how I perceive their ban. It seems thematically appropriate while still making roleplaying a Storm Lord quite fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2322-star-sage","name":"Star Sage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2322_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T06:19:12-07:00","id":258069,"title":"","content":"Glad to help! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And I second Merkonan's point - Tribes of the Moon is an <b>excellent </b>book all round, and it went a <i>long </i>way to forming my conception of the Iminir. The writer even specifically mentioned how they wanted to show off a lot more than the &quot;be the strongest, be the best&quot; ethos that seemed to dominate their representation so far.<br /> <br /> (The Blood Talons chapter was top-notch, too!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T09:16:41-07:00","id":258211,"title":"","content":"This is the most powerful example of upholding the Iminir's ban I've seen in Tribes of the Moon: <br /> <br /> <i>Depending on the circumstances, werewolves of the Iminir gain more renown and respect from their tribemates even if they lash out in rash reaction seeking revenge, rather than enduring quietly and planning a delayed vengeance. The Legend of the Warrior Al Altan is a perfect example of this. Ancient Mongolian tales tell of a soldier in the 1200s who was claimed by a demon when his family is threatened. <br /> In truth, Al Altan was a Storm Lord Cahalith who rode alongside Batu Khan of the Blue (and later Golden) Horde. Of all Batu Khan\u2019s warriors, Al Altan was the fiercest, and he still managed to conceal his true nature from many amongst his clan and the army he led. <br /> Al Altan was almost crippled by a sorcery-poisoned arrow in the back, which inflicted damage even his Uratha blood couldn\u2019t regenerate and reduced him to a lifetime of hesitant limping. The Storm Lord learned to guide his horse without the use of his legs, and trained to master the bow over sword and shield \u2014 since his balance was ruined after his injury, his skills in the melee of horseback warfare were limited.<br /> Three years later, he suffered horrific scarring and nerve damage from being burned by flaming arrows that set his robes aflame. Although he regenerated most of the damage to his flesh, he was left weak in body and prone to painful spasms. Thus his aim was ruined. When his fellow warriors (as well as his tribemates) looked upon him with pity, he ignored them all and trained his still-functioning right arm to hurl the spear as far as any other in the army. <br /> Al Altan died at the age of 40, while \u2018possessed by a demon.\u2019 To the Storm Lords, such ferocity was born of the warrior losing himself to his Rage, but the human witnesses had no such information to hone their perspective. When his camp was attacked, Al Altan limped out of his tent, spear in hand. He was the only warrior remaining, and as the women and children were cut down, he hurled spears, flaming brands from the cooking fires, clay pots and anything else within reach \u2014 each strike throwing an attacker from his horse. When there was nothing left to throw and his anger drowned all care of his dying people learning the truth of his nature, he changed to Gauru and leapt awkwardly at any rider who came within reach.<br /> By the end of the battle, he had killed more than 30 men, and was only finally brought down when three riders lanced him at the same moment in a coordinated attack. Even after death, even after losing the fight for his life, Al Altan inspires his tribe. In some parts of East Asia, variations on his rumored last words are still spoken as a curse to great enemies. \u2018You live only because I am too tired to kill you.'</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T11:56:58-07:00","id":258341,"title":"","content":"&quot;You only live because I'm too tired to kill you,&quot; is AWESOME!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T21:06:07-07:00","id":258650,"title":"","content":"Aaaaaaand, now I'm playing a Storm Lord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T02:12:55-07:00","id":258875,"title":"","content":"Some more Iminir goodness (Garret is the dude pictured in the corebook as the Storm Lord in their section with the badass sword):<br /> <br /> <i>Cassie wasn't breathing, so her lover breathed for her. Great mouthfuls of Garrett's breath rushed into Cassie's mouth and throat, inflating her lungs. He thumped down on her chest with rhythmic presses, staring into her open eyes all the while. When he wasn't breathing for girl he loved, Garrett was speaking to her with his usual gentle-voiced intensity. It worked when he gave orders. Now he hoped it would work as he begged.<br /> &quot;Don't die. Please, Cassie, don't die. It's not ending like this.&quot; Around him, Garrett's packmates looked on. Several shook their heads, and every one bore wounds from the fight. Their prey, their enemies, were scattered around the room in messy heaps. Cassie was no shifter, and her thin wolf's blood had done nothing to strengthen her weak heart. Now her lover was doing all he could to get it beating again.<br /> When she drew a gasping breath and went into spasms, the pack flinched back. Garrett immediately moved Cassie onto her side so she wouldn't swallow her tongue. A minute later and she was conscious again, weeping into his arms. He'd never felt such relief. He eventually rose from cradling her and walked over to the biggest corpse in the room. The spirit-thing was slowly dissolving, melting back into the Shadow. Even in death, the power in its form was enough for the beast to maintain a tenuous presence in the physical world. Garrett pulled the blade of his forefathers from the spirit's throat. It had been set there in the final strike of the fight \u2014the killing blow.<br /> His pack looked at him; the same awe projecting out, the same question standing in each pair of eyes. What now? &quot;Let's get out of here,&quot; Garrett said. He was alpha. He knew best. They nodded and obeyed, silent as wolves in the wild.</i><br /> <hr /><br /> <i>Empathy<br /> Garrett looked at his packmates. Only an hour before, they\u2019d seen him slay the ugliest murder-spirit any of them had ever seen, then bring Cassie back to life by CPR. He looked around and saw them looking back at him. They wanted another miracle. They wanted another miracle, or they were all dead.<br /> Elliot wanted to fight. Elliot always wanted to fight, and he wasn't going to take any other option this time. He was a Talon; he was made for moments like this. Joanna was an Irraka of the Hunters. She could vanish into the city like she\u2019d never been born, and Garrett knew she wanted to right now. Charles was like Garrett \u2014 the alpha knew the other man\u2019s thoughts were on his wife, just as Garrett\u2019s own had been fixed on getting back to Cassie when news of the Pure assault on the city had filtered through the packs.<br /> He weighed up their options, and made his decision. \u201cWe follow Joanna to Charles\u2019s house, where we get his wife and get the hell out of the city. Jo, we need to go the blackest, darkest ways to get there \u2014 through this world and the next \u2014 but we need to get there fast.\u201d Before Elliot could murmur his disappointed growl, Garrett turned to him. \u201cRemember that Talon lodge you crossed back in October? The ones in the next town over who said they\u2019d only speak with us again if you beat their best in a duel?\u201d Elliot nodded. Garrett continued.<br /> \u201cThe time\u2019s come. We need their help, and that means you need to fight like you've never fought before.\u201d Elliot was silent for a time, then said, \u201cI\u2019ll need my father\u2019s sword. It\u2019s at my apartment.\u201d<br /> Garrett shook his head. \u201cI've seen you slay demons without it, my friend. And I\u2019ll see you beat your tribemate senseless tonight without it as well. If I didn't think you could do it, I\u2019d choose another, easier way. Our lives ride on the outcome of that fight, El. And I know you can do it. Now\u2026 everyone ready?\u201d Everyone nodded, and the pack moved like hounds snapped at their heels. Now they had purpose.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}